; Cover the scenario when the Reader cannot infer the pointee type of
; a byval/sret argument of an indirect call, when untyped pointers are used.

; In this test the result of an OpLoad, which is an untyped pointer, is used as
; the function argument with byval attribute; getTypedPtrFromUntypedOperand()
; can't infer the pointee type from OpLoad, so it errors out.

; RUN: llvm-spirv %s -to-binary -o %t.spv
; RUN: not llvm-spirv -r %t.spv 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

; CHECK: Cannot infer the pointee type of an untyped pointer argument with type attribute of an indirect call

119734787 65536 393230 13 0
2 Capability Addresses
2 Capability Linkage
2 Capability Kernel
2 Capability Int8
2 Capability UntypedPointersKHR
2 Capability FunctionPointersINTEL
8 Extension "SPV_INTEL_function_pointers"
8 Extension "SPV_KHR_untyped_pointers"
5 ExtInstImport 1 "OpenCL.std"
3 MemoryModel 2 2
4 Name 7 "helper"
3 Name 8 "pp"
3 Name 9 "fp"
3 Name 11 "p"
6 Decorate 7 LinkageAttributes "helper" Export
5 Decorate 12 ArgumentAttributeINTEL 0 2
4 TypeInt 3 8 0
2 TypeVoid 2
3 TypeUntypedPointerKHR 4 7
5 TypeFunction 5 2 4 4
5 Function 2 7 0 5
3 FunctionParameter 4 8
3 FunctionParameter 4 9
2 Label 10
4 Load 4 11 8
5 FunctionPointerCallINTEL 2 12 9 11
1 Return
1 FunctionEnd
